+# Beat my track terms and conditions draft
+
+**Draft for publisher and regional legal review. Not effective or published.**
+
+Proposed version: `bmt-terms-draft-2026-10-24-r2`. Effective date: **[TO BE SET AFTER REVIEW]**.
+
+These terms cover Beat my track, online racing, creation/sharing and available purchases. They explain player conduct, service changes and what happens when something goes wrong.
+
+## 1 Publisher and contact
+
+The publisher is **[LEGAL PUBLISHER NAME]**, established in **[COUNTRY]**, registration **[NUMBER OR NOT APPLICABLE]**, business/contact address **[PUBLIC ADDRESS]**. “We”, “us” and “our” mean that publisher, which supplies the game services described here.
+
+An individual purchase may have a different seller or payment provider depending on the store/country. The checkout and confirmation identify their roles. This does not remove obligations the law places on us.
+
+Support/complaints: **[SUPPORT EMAIL]**. Privacy: **[PRIVACY EMAIL]**. Security: **[SECURITY EMAIL]**. Illegal-content notices: **[PUBLIC NOTICE URL OR EMAIL]**. Authority contact and languages: **[AUTHORITY CONTACT AND LANGUAGES]**. These may share a monitored contact channel.
+
+Legal information: **[LEGAL PAGE URL]**. Privacy: **[PRIVACY URL]**. Community rules: **[COMMUNITY RULES URL]**. External account deletion: **[ACCOUNT DELETION URL]**.
+
+## 2 Agreement and mandatory rights
+
+You must be able to read and save these terms before agreeing. Purchase descriptions and checkout information form part of each purchase agreement. The community rules govern public conduct and sharing. Agreeing to these terms is not consent to optional analytics or advertising.
+
+Mandatory rights prevail over any inconsistent clause, including rights concerning delivery, defects, refunds, personal data, complaints and access to courts or authorities.
+
+## 3 Age and launch markets
+
+You must be at least **13 years old** to use the game. Initial distribution markets are the **European Union, United States and Canada**.
+
+Meeting this minimum age does not establish independent legal capacity for every feature, purchase or personal-data choice. Obtain parental/guardian authorisation where the applicable law requires it and complete any required authorisation process. A content rating, Google account or payment confirmation does not replace that process.
+
+Minors may make purchases only as local law permits or with the required authorisation. Repeated small purchases may need to be considered together. Some countries require parental consent for particular personal-data processing even after age 13; the applicable privacy process must respect those differences.
+
+## 4 Licence and requirements
+
+We grant a personal, non-exclusive licence to use the game for its intended purposes. We and our licensors retain rights in its software and supplied assets. Applicable third-party/open-source licences and mandatory legal rights remain unaffected.
+
+You may share ordinary gameplay recordings, screenshots and live streams, including monetised videos/streams, under the game rights we control. This does not authorise third-party music we cannot license, distribution of standalone game assets/software, false endorsement or infringement of another person's privacy.
+
+The listing states device/software requirements. Online accounts, publication and verified competition need compatible service versions and connectivity. Offline availability depends on the installed version and locally available content.
+
+Ordinary racing has no paid retry or energy requirement. Current optional products do not sell competitive vehicle performance. Recipients are not charged for ordinary racing on a shared track.
+
+## 5 Accounts and recovery
+
+Use sign-in honestly, protect access to your identity provider, and report suspected misuse. You are responsible for your conduct, not automatically for every unauthorised action by someone else.
+
+Real purchases require an identified, signed-in game account; guests cannot use paid checkout. The same account on another supported device can recover benefits and information actually held by the service. This is not a complete device backup: local drafts, records, caches and settings may need separate backup or transfer.
+
+Recovery of a consumed publishing pack restores remaining verified allocations, not the original pack a second time. Keep backups of valuable local drafts using available export/save facilities. We remain responsible for security/recovery measures required by law. Account deletion has different consequences under section 12.
+
+## 6 Fair play and competition
+
+Do not fabricate results, manipulate race/payment evidence, cheat, impersonate others or deliberately disrupt the service. Mandatory interoperability and research rights remain unaffected.
+
+Results follow the relevant content/rules version and evidence checks. On reasonable grounds, we may investigate, hold, reject or correct a suspected invalid result. Handling/rule changes may create separate records instead of converting historical results. Purchases guarantee no ranking, matchmaking outcome, reward eligibility or prize.
+
+Account/content actions follow section 11. We cannot promise prevention or immediate detection of every cheat.
+
+## 7 Player contributions and sharing permissions
+
+Supplied road pieces, vehicles, scenery, textures, audio and software remain ours or our licensors'. You retain rights in your original layouts and other original contributions to the extent they receive legal protection. Using supplied assets does not transfer ownership of those assets.
+
+Submit only content you have the right to share. Do not include protected work, confidential information or personal data without an appropriate right/legal basis. Follow the community rules.
+
+When you choose to submit, publish or share content, you grant a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence to host, reproduce, technically adapt, display and distribute it as needed for those features. This includes track previews/downloads, public/private challenges, authorised ghost playback, relevant leaderboard/profile information, podium appearances, moderation and compatibility processing. We respect the feature's disclosed audience/privacy controls; private submission alone does not authorise public distribution. Other players may race/use deliberately shared tracks through the intended features.
+
+Service providers and a successor under section 19 may use this licence for the same purposes and within the same limits. It does not transfer ownership of your contributions or permit unrelated sales or AI training. External advertising featuring a player's original contribution requires separate permission or another applicable right.
+
+Previously downloaded copies may remain after removal. Continued retention/use remains subject to personal-data rights and any mandatory content-retrieval rights.
+
+## 8 Purchases and entitlements
+
+Only release-store products actually offered can be purchased. Checkout identifies the seller/provider, product, total price, duration and conditions; the displayed prices/currency must match provider checkout. Simulations do not take payment.
+
+Confirm the game account before checkout. Paid benefits attach to that account. Pending, cancelled or unverified transactions grant nothing. Contact support about an undelivered confirmed payment.
+
+The following descriptions reflect the current entitlement model and must match release checkout before sales:
+
+| Product | Benefit |
+| --- | --- |
+| 1 publishing slot | One additional single-use publishing allocation. |
+| 5 publishing slots | Five additional single-use publishing allocations. |
+| 10 publishing slots | Ten additional single-use publishing allocations. |
+| One month ad-free | One calendar month of the ad-free/resume benefits below, without automatic renewal. |
+| Permanent ad-free | The same benefits without a scheduled entitlement expiry while the relevant service is supplied. This does not promise lifetime hosting/maintenance; section 14 and mandatory remedies apply. |
+
+Eligible accounts start with one initial free publishing allocation, not a monthly allowance. Successful non-exempt publication consumes one allocation, including a new published revision. Same-version retries and failed/unverified publications consume none. Spent allocations are not reusable; hiding/removing a track, including moderation removal, does not automatically return them. Unused purchased allocations have no scheduled expiry while the account/relevant service remain available, subject to sections 9, 11, 12 and 14.
+
+Active ad-free access suppresses automatic interruption ads and allows the standard race resumes without rewarded ads or spending banked/daily resumes. The maximum remains three resumes per race. It does not add publishing capacity or unlimited resumes. Any separate future rewarded offer must clearly state its benefit without contradicting purchased rights.
+
+Monthly expiry uses UTC: add one calendar month to the later of existing monthly expiry or verified grant time, keeping the time of day and clamping to the target month's last day. For example, 31 January 2027 at 12:00 UTC becomes 28 February at 12:00 UTC; adding another month to that expiry gives 28 March, not 31 March. Show the resulting expiry in the account/store. Each verified purchase extends once. Permanent access takes precedence.
+
+Earned Coins and racing points have no cash redemption/transfer function offered by us; this does not remove statutory repayment/compensation rights. Current products do not sell Coins or XP.
+
+## 9 Withdrawal refunds and defects
+
+Mandatory withdrawal and defect remedies remain available. Digital delivery or consumption does not itself remove them. Where immediate digital-content supply can lawfully end a withdrawal right, checkout must obtain the required prior express consent, acknowledgement and durable confirmation. Continuing services may follow different rules.
+
+**[BEFORE SALES: COMPLETE EACH PRODUCT'S CONTENT/SERVICE CLASSIFICATION, IMMEDIATE SUPPLY PROCESS, CONFIRMATION AND WITHDRAWAL/REFUND PROCEDURE.]** Part use of a publishing allocation or timed benefit does not eliminate every remedy.
+
+Use the store's refund process or contact **[SUPPORT EMAIL]** with the order reference/problem. The withdrawal function for contracts with an applicable withdrawal right is **[WITHDRAWAL URL OR APPROVED PROVIDER FLOW]**. You may also send a clear withdrawal request through the available contacts.
+
+Verified refunds/reversals may change the affected entitlement. We explain changes, avoid duplicate reversals and preserve unrelated legitimate progress. We impose no penalty for exercising a legal right. A justified restriction for your material breach does not itself create a discretionary goodwill-refund entitlement; section 11 preserves applicable legal, contractual and store rights.
+
+## 10 Ads and optional processing
+
+The listing and purchase descriptions identify ads and ad-free benefits. Automatic interstitials appear at permitted breaks, not during active driving. Rewarded offers explain the interaction and reward before you choose them; cancelled, failed or unavailable ads do not count as completed offers.
+
+The privacy notice and applicable consent process govern advertising and optional analytics. Terms acceptance is not that consent. Privacy choices must be changeable through the disclosed controls.
+
+## 11 Conduct reporting and account bans
+
+The rules cover racing/profile names, track names/descriptions/layouts/content, challenges, car appearances, reports/appeals and other service use. They prohibit offensive/abusive content, hate/discrimination, explicit sexual material, threats, unlawful defamation, bullying, harassment, private-information disclosure, impersonation, fraud, cheating and deliberate disruption. Disguising prohibited content with symbols, spelling or track shapes, malicious reporting, evading restrictions and other material breaches are also prohibited.
+
+We assess evidence and context. An allegation, disliked name, strong competitive result or ordinary collision is not automatically a breach. Good-faith criticism, complaints, appeals and refund requests are not misconduct merely because they challenge us.
+
+Use in-game reporting or send an illegal-content notice to **[PUBLIC NOTICE URL OR EMAIL]**; no game account is required for that notice. Identify the content, concern and relevant information.
+
+For a material breach, unlawful content, reasonably evidenced fraud/cheating, security threat or binding legal requirement, we may require a name/content change, remove/hide content, exclude invalid results, restrict features, suspend an account or permanently ban/terminate access. Action must be proportionate to seriousness, harm, repetition and circumstances. Serious/repeated misconduct or urgent risks may justify immediate action without warning. Purchases do not provide immunity from enforcement.
+
+We provide legally required/permitted reasons, notice and review/redress information. Request review through **[SUPPORT EMAIL OR REVIEW URL]** or the available appeal process. Applicable store, consumer, regulatory and court remedies remain available.
+
+A lawful ban may prevent access to account-dependent paid benefits. We do not offer goodwill refunds solely because proportionate enforcement of your material breach prevents access. This is not automatic forfeiture of every unrelated entitlement or exclusion of a remedy required by law, the purchase agreement or store rules. We assess the affected benefit, explain the decision and review mistaken/disproportionate sanctions.
+
+## 12 Account deletion
+
+Request deletion in the game or at **[ACCOUNT DELETION URL]**. The privacy notice explains erasure, lawful retention and requests concerning retained personal content.
+
+Deletion permanently closes the account and erases its entitlement records, including unused allocations and monthly/permanent ad-free access. Normal recovery cannot restore the deleted account/erased benefits; later Google sign-in creates a new game account. Disclose this before confirmation. Where possible, seek purchase recovery/refunds before deletion.
+
+Deletion does not waive outstanding legal claims or applicable store remedies. A provider receipt may still support a remedy; deletion itself does not promise restoration to a new account. It does not delete your Google account or local files. A future renewing product would require separate cancellation information; the current monthly product does not renew automatically.
+
+## 13 Updates and major gameplay changes
+
+We may update, rebalance, redesign, replace or retire features, including changes that substantially alter gameplay. Valid reasons include improving balance in response to feedback/observed use, introducing new mechanics/content/formats, correcting defects or unfair advantages, legal/security compliance, compatibility changes and evidenced capacity/cost/operational needs. Each change needs an identified valid reason and must meet applicable legal conditions.
+
+Changes may affect physics, handling, controls, cameras, tracks, rules, competitions, scoring/rankings, progression/rewards, presentation, the editor or online services. We do not promise indefinite retention of a particular historical experience, subject to existing commitments and mandatory rights. Successors remain bound by the same conditions.
+
+Changes beyond those needed for conformity require clear information and no additional charge for the change itself. A distinct paid product requires a separate offer/agreement; this clause cannot convert an existing purchase into a subscription or arbitrarily confiscate benefits/progress. Explain relevant effects on saved content and purchases.
+
+For a more than minor negative effect on access/use, we will give the required advance information on a durable medium and explain the applicable free termination/remedy route or option to retain an unchanged conforming service. Necessary update duties remain.
+
+## 14 Outages and discontinuation
+
+Maintenance, incidents and dependencies may interrupt online features. We will give practicable notice of planned material interruptions and take reasonable restoration steps; no separate personal-player uptime SLA is offered.
+
+We may discontinue online services for legitimate operational, technical, legal or commercial reasons, including commercial unsustainability, costs the game cannot reasonably support, or inability to continue necessary technical/operational arrangements. This does not override existing commitments or consumer rights; hosting/maintenance is not promised indefinitely.
+
+**[BEFORE PUBLICATION: SET PLANNED SHUTDOWN NOTICE PERIOD AND CHANNELS.]** We will give that notice and any longer legally required notice before planned closure, explaining the features/date, paid benefits, outstanding orders, content retrieval and personal data. Urgent legal/security or comparable unavoidable reasons may require earlier action. We will stop sales of benefits that cannot be supplied as agreed and provide required remedies. Necessary update obligations must also be addressed.
+
+Shutdown may end sign-in, discovery/downloads, verification, rankings/competitions, synchronisation and online purchases/rewards. Offline features may continue where supported by the installed version, local content and compatible devices; not every feature is guaranteed to survive. Apply required retrieval and privacy arrangements.
+
+Disclose these limits prominently before purchase, particularly for permanent ad-free and publishing offers. A non-expiring entitlement is not lifetime hosting and does not waive remedies when service ends.
+
+## 15 Bugs and realistic service limits
+
+We aim for reliable, secure play but cannot guarantee uninterrupted availability, absence of every defect, universal compatibility or prevention of all cheating/unwanted content. No particular competitive outcome or enjoyment is guaranteed.
+
+We remain responsible for agreed functionality, quality, security, updates and applicable remedies. General bug language is not acceptance of an undisclosed defect. A specific deviation may be agreed only where lawful and clearly identified, with any required express separate acceptance before contracting.
+
+## 16 Liability
+
+We remain liable as applicable law requires. Where fair and lawful, we exclude loss not reasonably foreseeable when contracting, loss not caused by conduct for which we are legally responsible, and business loss from commercial use outside the agreed game purpose. Permitted gameplay videos/streams do not reduce mandatory consumer protections.
+
+We do not exclude liability for fraud, deliberate wrongdoing, gross negligence, prohibited death/personal-injury exclusions, mandatory consumer/privacy rights or any liability that cannot lawfully be limited. Statutory repair, refund, price-reduction and compensation rights remain.
+
+## 17 Complaints law and disputes
+
+Contact **[SUPPORT EMAIL]** with the issue, account/order reference and requested remedy, without passwords, tokens or full card details. We investigate/respond within applicable legal periods. There is no artificial contractual complaint deadline or duty to delay urgent legal action.
+
+Support languages and regional arrangements: **[SUPPORT LANGUAGES AND MARKET CONTACT ARRANGEMENTS]**. Legal documents, disclosures and support must match launch territories, including applicable French-language requirements for Quebec. Any required French contract version must be provided before a legally valid choice of another language; this English draft alone does not fulfil that process.
+
+Finnish law governs without removing applicable mandatory protections of the consumer's habitual residence. Any competent court remains available; no exclusive Finnish venue or mandatory consumer arbitration is imposed.
+
+Finnish consumers may contact [Consumer Advisory Services](https://www.kkv.fi/en/consumer-affairs/consumer-advisory-services/) and submit eligible disputes to the [Consumer Disputes Board](https://www.kuluttajariita.fi/en/). Others may use the competent local assistance/dispute body. Privacy, regulatory and content-redress routes remain available.
+
+## 18 Changes to these terms
+
+We may propose changes for section 13's valid reasons or clarification without reducing existing rights. We will explain material changes, effective dates, advance notice and applicable choice/termination rights, and seek fresh agreement where required. Continued use does not replace required express consent.
+
+Purchase-specific terms continue for existing orders unless lawfully changed. An invalid term does not automatically become the maximum restriction legally possible; the remainder continues only as law permits.
+
+## 19 Sale transfer and successor operators
+
+We may sell, assign, license or transfer the game business and IP/assets we own or may transfer, including name/branding, code, artwork, audio and documentation, through a sale, merger, reorganisation or other lawful arrangement. Third-party and player rights remain protected.
+
+We may appoint others to maintain, develop, publish, support or operate the game. Delegation alone does not release our obligations. A player-contract transfer must be legally effective, preserve consumer guarantees as required and include the successor assuming affected commitments and any necessary notice/agreement. Identify the new party/contact/effective date when required. Transfer alone waives no existing claim or paid benefit.
+
+Section 7 permissions may pass with the business for the same operating/development purposes and limits, without transferring ownership of players' contributions.
+
+Data disclosure/handover needs a lawful basis, transparency, minimisation, security and relevant international-transfer safeguards. Identify the responsible controller and update notices where required. Terms acceptance is not blanket consent to unrelated data use. Successor changes remain subject to sections 13 and 18.
